# f04 -- READ COMMITTED: a write cannot skip the re-read.
#
# T2's write is refused with `updated`. Trying again without
# readlatest is refused again: sm1 does not let the caller lose
# the predicate. The refusal is not an abort: T2 is still
# active and still holds the row lock, so T3 stays queued behind
# it until T2 ends.


== pairing RR/RR == T1=RC T2=RC T3=RC
@1 T1 begin -> ok
@1 T2 begin -> ok
@2 T1 write R1 1 -> ok
@3 T2 write R1 2 blocks -> blocked
@4 T1 commit -> ok
@3 T2 write R1 2 blocks -> updated (resumed)
@5 check last T2 updated -> satisfied
@6 T3 begin -> ok
@7 T3 write R1 3 blocks -> blocked
@8 T2 write R1 2 -> updated
@8 check last T2 updated -> satisfied
@9 T2 abort -> ok
@7 T3 write R1 3 blocks -> ok (resumed)
@10 check last T3 ok -> satisfied
@11 T3 commit -> ok
@12 check committed T1 T3 -> satisfied
@12 check row R1 3 -> satisfied
